# ERP Unite

For the project manager who needs to speak the language.

<div class="byline">Project manager pack · product literacy · what it does · the vocabulary that matters</div>

---

<!-- _class: stat -->

<div class="number">enough to lead</div>

## not a configuration manual

You won't configure ERP Unite. You'll run meetings where business owners ask about it, functional consultants describe it, and customers compare it to alternatives. **This pack makes those meetings yours to lead.**

---

# What ERP Unite is — the one-paragraph version

If a customer asks "what does this thing do?" — say this.

> *"ERP Unite is the finance layer for an insurance brokerage. It takes commission statements from carriers, applies the cash to the right invoices, runs producer compensation calculations, handles month-end accruals and journals, and posts to your general ledger. It sits between your agency management system and your GL — neither of which it replaces."*

That's the elevator pitch. Everything else in this pack expands on it.

