# The four moving parts

Internally, ERP Unite is four applications sharing one database. Customers experience them as one product.

<div class="cols two">
<div class="card">

### **Cash Hub**
The first app a customer sees. Statement ingestion, cash application matching, journals, accruals, collections.

</div>
<div class="card">

### **Compensation Hub**
Where producer pay happens. Compensation actuals, producer comp rules, split intake, audit log.

</div>
</div>

<div class="cols two">
<div class="card">

### **Producer Portal**
External-facing. Producers sign in to see their own splits and reports. Self-service for the broker's commissioned staff.

</div>
<div class="card">

### **Integration Hub**
The plumbing. Six Azure Function apps connecting Unite to Accounting Hub, FinOps, Workday, Mulesoft. Invisible to users; critical to operations.

</div>
</div>

