# The vocabulary that matters

Twenty terms. Master them and you can lead any conversation.

---

# Vocabulary — the Cash Hub side

The terms a Cash Hub user says in every meeting.

| Term | What it means |
|------|---------------|
| **Statement** | A commission report from a carrier — usually monthly |
| **Statement Header** | The record of one received statement |
| **Statement Line** | One row from inside a statement — typically one policy or one customer |
| **Template** | The saved recipe for parsing a specific carrier's format |
| **Mapping Studio** | The AI-assisted authoring interface for templates |
| **Provider** | A carrier or other source of statements (Aetna, MetLife, etc.) |
| **Cash Application** | The process of matching statement lines to products + customers in the GL |
| **Match Rule** | A learned rule that auto-matches a statement pattern to a product |
| **Approve to AH** | The button that sends matched cash to the Accounting Hub |
| **Research Case** | An investigation record for cash that can't be matched automatically |

*Memorize these. Use them. Customers and consultants will use these terms — don't get caught reaching for them.*

---

# Vocabulary — the Compensation side

The terms a CompHub user says in every meeting.

| Term | What it means |
|------|---------------|
| **Party** | A person in the system — usually a producer, sometimes an external user |
| **Producer** | A salesperson who earns commission |
| **Producer Comp Rule** | The rate this producer gets, for this product, in this renewal year |
| **Split Intake** (SIF) | A record of how commission splits across multiple producers for an account |
| **Cost Center Allocation** | How the split's GL impact is distributed across cost centers |
| **Compensation Batch** | A periodic run that computes producer payables |
| **Compensation Actual** | One line of the batch — what a specific producer is owed |
| **Invoice ID** | A generated identifier that ties the producer payable to the AH posting |
| **Workflow Status** | Where a record sits in its approval lifecycle (NotSubmitted, Submitted, Approved) |
| **Accrual Batch** | A cost-center-and-month grouping of computed accruals |

*The SIF lifecycle (NotSubmitted → Submitted → InProgress → Approved) is the most-asked-about workflow in customer engagements. Learn it.*

---

