# Questions you should be able to answer

The customer asks; you respond.

---

# Customer Q&A — your shortlist

If a customer asks any of these, have the answer ready.

- **"How does it know what's in our carrier statements?"** → Templates. Authored once per carrier via Mapping Studio with AI assist.
- **"Will our producers see other producers' commissions?"** → No. Permission scopes by region, market, P&amp;L, and cost center.
- **"Can we keep our existing GL?"** → Yes. Unite posts journals out; doesn't replace the ledger.
- **"What happens when a carrier changes their format?"** → A super user re-runs Mapping Studio for that template; takes minutes, not days.
- **"What's the AI doing exactly?"** → Suggesting column mappings during template authoring. Humans approve every line. Every inference is logged.
- **"How do we audit a write-off?"** → Collections Case carries the full investigation history; the generated journal carries the case reference.
- **"Can a producer fix their own splits?"** → They submit changes through the Portal; an internal user approves; system versions the change.

*Net: these are the recurring questions in every implementation. Practice the answers.*

---

# Escalation cues — when to call a functional consultant

You don't need to answer everything. You need to recognize when to escalate.

- **"How do we configure X?"** → That's functional. Pull in the Cash or Comp consultant for the answer.
- **"What's the data model for Y?"** → Technical / EA. Pull in the architect.
- **"What's the integration latency to AH?"** → Integration lead.
- **"Can it do Z that our current system does?"** → Fit/gap conversation. Schedule a discovery session.
- **"What's the ROI?"** → Business case. Pull in the engagement lead with the value framework from the sales pack.

*PM action:* know who's on speed-dial for each cue. You're the orchestrator, not the encyclopedia.

